      "experiment_id": "SUPTRNA-SAFETY",
      "question": "Does a suppressor tRNA also read through the body's normal stop codons, and how much?",
      "why_it_matters": "A therapy that gets past the patient's premature stop but also runs past thousands of normal stops is producing extended proteins everywhere. The safety atlas measures this for G418 and for nothing else.",
      "what_the_lab_does": "Ribosome profiling of cells expressing a suppressor tRNA, measuring occupancy past every normal stop codon in the transcriptome rather than at the target variant.",
      "comparison": "Suppressor tRNA against the same delivery construct without it, three replicates per arm.",
      "success_criterion": "There is no success direction here. The output is a measured burden across normal stops, reported whatever it is.",
      "if_it_fails": "A high burden would constrain which designs are usable and would change the coverage frontier's recommendations, which currently optimise reach without a measured safety cost for this modality.",
      "evidence_gap_reason": "The native-stop atlas exists only for G418. The safety layer for suppressor tRNAs is prediction with no measurement behind it.",
      "assay": "Ribosome profiling, native-stop occupancy across the transcriptome",
      "model_system": "A human cell line tolerant of sustained suppressor tRNA expression",
